.env
node_modules
# package-lock.json IS tracked on purpose: the Dockerfile runs `npm ci` against
# it. Untracked, a rebuild resolves dependencies fresh and can break unchanged
# code (2026-07-28: supabase-js 2.111.0 pulled in, needs Node 22).
# Claude Code runtime state. `.claude/` itself IS tracked on purpose:
# kit-owned files are regenerable via `init.sh --update`, but settings.json
# (accumulated permission approvals) and protected-paths (project no-touch
# zones) are project truth that nothing can rebuild. Only machine-local
# state is excluded.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
